# Standard-library stubs: methods package (S4).
#
# Declaration-only stub file (`.Rtypes`); see base.Rtypes for the format. The S4 machinery is dynamic — class
# membership and coercion results depend on runtime class definitions and dispatch — so almost everything
# is widened to `Any`. Stubbing the names still resolves them and keeps strict mode from flagging them.
# (S4 class, generic, and method *names* are tracked separately as string literals, not through these
# bindings.)

# widened to Any: each return is dynamic — it depends on a runtime class or argument value, not on the
# argument *types*, so a static return would be falsely precise.
# - `is(object)` returns the class vector while `is(object, class2)` returns a logical (arity-dependent).
# - `as(object, Class)` and `new(Class, ...)` return an object of the runtime-named class.
# - `validObject` returns its argument if valid (shape mirrors the input).
# - `setClass`/`setGeneric`/`setMethod`/`setValidity`/`setRefClass` return S4 machinery objects (a class
#   generator, the generic/method name, a class representation) tied to the dynamic dispatch system.
is : Any
as : Any
new : Any
validObject : Any
setClass : Any
setGeneric : Any
setMethod : Any
setValidity : Any
setRefClass : Any

# Single-logical class predicates with a fixed signature.
isVirtualClass : fn(Class: character) -> logical
extends : fn(class1: character, class2: character) -> logical
